Error: Jet.ComptimeConstructNotSupported: `LEXED` holds a compiler value (`CompilerLexed`), which exists only while compiling
  --> Tests/UI/CompilerAPI/compiler_value_read_at_runtime_is_rejected_2.jet:9:11
    |
  9 |     print(LEXED.tokens.len())
    |           ^^^^^
 Why: Comptime code and `build: fn` read compiler values; the running program has no compiler to answer them
 Fix: Compute the plain value you need (a Bool, number or String) inside a `#run` block and read that at runtime
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ComptimeConstructNotSupported
